Standards Organisation of Nigeria Act, 2015 - Section 4: Functions and powers of the Council
General Provisions
(1) The Council shall be the governing body of the Organisation and shall have responsibility for—
(a) advising the Federal Government on national policy on standards, standardization, quality control and metrology;
(b) designating, establishing and approving national standards in respect of metrology, materials, commodities, structures and processes;
(c) providing quality control measures for raw materials and finished products locally manufactured or imported into Nigeria;
(d) overseeing the overall administration and financial management of the Organisation.

sections.full_text:
(1) The Organisation shall establish and maintain a fund from which shall be defrayed all expenditure incurred by the Organisation.
(2) There shall be paid and credited to the fund established under subsection (1) of this section—
(a) budgetary allocations and subventions from the Federal Government;
(b) fees charged and revenue earned for services, certifications and laboratory analyses rendered by the Organisation;
(c) gifts, loans, grants-in-aid, testamentary dispositions and endowments from international organizations or partners.
